READS the TRANSITION: the N where 'first-gap nonempty' flips to 'empty' is the n-specific
crossover. At/after it, the shrinking window (~1/2N^2) outruns the densest base's ladder =>
no integer outlier lands in-gap. N=12 (LRC14) should be on the empty side.
